      "id": "cmsfkfv0d000a04jocufgwpdx",
      "term": "Give me more details on assets, liabilities, and equity",
      "setTitle": "Accounting - \"Talking\"",
      "klps": [
        {
          "text": "The accounting equation, Assets = Liabilities + Equity, serves as the foundation for the balance sheet structure.",
          "kind": "definition"
        },
        {
          "text": "Assets are resources controlled by the entity that are expected to generate future economic benefits or cash inflows.",
          "kind": "definition"
        },
        {
          "text": "Liabilities represent external claims against those assets, requiring future cash outflows to settle these obligations.",
          "kind": "mechanism"
        },
        {
          "text": "Equity represents the owners' residual claim, consisting of contributed capital and earnings retained in the business over time.",
          "kind": "definition"
        },
        {
          "text": "Liabilities and equity together represent the two primary capital structures used to fund the acquisition of productive assets.",
          "kind": "causal"
        }
      ],
